Vista: lock an allocation only for the length of one CPU access. Vista shows
the CPU what the GPU wrote only through a lock taken after the write, so a
mapping kept from an earlier lock reads old data. Every map now takes a
fresh lock and every unmap releases it. The staging pool, which keeps one
lock for its whole life, is switched off by clearing the copy-transfer caps.

